@Veritasium What you see in the grating demo is the diffuse reflection of the laser head.

If you did the math, you would find the laser's amplitude is too confined to have such a strong contribution from the grating. If you say your laser is collimated to 1 mm the contribution and there is about 300 mm from the point where the laser "hits" to the edge of the grating (like at 30:22), the amplitude of the laser at that point is less than 10^-50. You won't be able to distinguish that from the noise of your camera. 

At 29:50 you can see the differences in the Poynting between the laser and the diffuse reflections. At 30:22 it is clear that the diffuse reflection is within an order of magnitude of the brightness of the laser on the paper. Diffuse reflections behave identically to the uncollimated source used earlier, so the demo is not illustrating what you present.

This is why I’m a panpsychist, optimization is the essence of existence and the essence of optimization is computation. This is just stochastic convergence; 

“Suppose that a random number generator generates a pseudorandom floating point number between 0 and 1. Let random variable X represent the distribution of possible outputs by the algorithm. Because the pseudorandom number is generated deterministically, its next value is not truly random. Suppose that as you observe a sequence of randomly generated numbers, you can deduce a pattern and make increasingly accurate predictions as to what the next randomly generated number will be. Let Xn be your guess of the value of the next random number after observing the first n random numbers. As you learn the pattern and your guesses become more accurate, not only will the distribution of Xn converge to the distribution of X, but the outcomes of Xn will converge to the outcomes of X.”

Self-organizing criticality is how our brain dynamics generate topological order, and subsequently brain waves. Self-organizing criticality is universal in all of nature, and is present in at least one of every theory of each emergent scale. There are self-organizing theories of consciousness, of quantum->classical emergence, and of spacetime itself via quantum loop gravity.
